1
00:00:01,635 --> 00:00:04,905
Defeating the Heli-Tornado

2
00:00:06,099 --> 00:00:07,559
What?!

3
00:00:07,559 --> 00:00:09,319
You were just bluffing?!

4
00:00:09,319 --> 00:00:12,775
Yeah! I just said the first thing that came to mind.

5
00:00:12,775 --> 00:00:14,506
But why would you do that?

6
00:00:14,506 --> 00:00:17,932
Oh yeah?! Well, I have a secret weapon that can beat your Heli-Tornado! (FX-italic)

7
00:00:17,932 --> 00:00:20,652
Why did you have to say that?!

8
00:00:20,652 --> 00:00:23,378
It was the only way to get out of that situation...

9
00:00:23,378 --> 00:00:25,202
Juuun!

10
00:00:25,202 --> 00:00:28,530
Don't worry. I'll think of a plan starting now.

11
00:00:28,530 --> 00:00:30,469
What are you two talking about?

12
00:00:31,170 --> 00:00:32,527
Vera?

13
00:00:32,527 --> 00:00:34,551
It's none of your business.

14
00:00:34,551 --> 00:00:35,817
Oh, really?

15
00:00:36,618 --> 00:00:38,213
I think it is.

16
00:00:41,216 --> 00:00:42,551
Aah!

17
00:00:43,944 --> 00:00:45,524
Here's the thing.

18
00:00:45,524 --> 00:00:48,286
We were filming a dance video by the Mowtown docks yesterday.

19
00:00:48,286 --> 00:00:52,973
When robots came out of nowhere and started fighting, I quickly got out my camera.

20
00:00:52,973 --> 00:00:55,671
And that's when I saw two familiar faces.

21
00:00:55,671 --> 00:00:57,194
Care to explain?

22
00:00:58,279 --> 00:01:00,268
Uhh... maybe they were guys that just look like us?

23
00:01:00,268 --> 00:01:05,686
That's right! They say there are at least three people in the world that look exactly like you!

24
00:01:08,022 --> 00:01:11,233
Wearing the same clothes, with the same hair, and the same shoes?!

25
00:01:11,233 --> 00:01:13,843
You expect me to buy that story?! Really?!

26
00:01:13,843 --> 00:01:15,786
We're late for something!! Gotta go!

27
00:01:16,525 --> 00:01:18,771
Hey! Get back here!

28
00:01:24,186 --> 00:01:27,150
What do we do? We can't keep running away from them!

29
00:01:27,150 --> 00:01:30,489
We just have to figure out a way to steal that video from Vera!

30
00:01:30,489 --> 00:01:33,698
Well... she could have saved other copies.

31
00:01:33,698 --> 00:01:37,170
And if she uploads it to the Internet, there's nothing we can do at that point.

32
00:01:38,545 --> 00:01:42,268
Don't worry about a thing! I have a great idea!

33
00:01:43,140 --> 00:01:45,984
That just makes me worry more...

34
00:01:51,418 --> 00:01:53,426
Good day, everyone.

35
00:01:53,426 --> 00:01:58,158
I would like to address the rumors going around regarding a giant robot.

36
00:01:58,158 --> 00:01:59,718
Giant robot?

37
00:01:59,718 --> 00:02:00,829
Yes!

38
00:02:00,829 --> 00:02:02,680
There have been reported sightings of robots in

39
00:02:02,680 --> 00:02:07,376
concrete channels, under highways, and flying above the city,

40
00:02:07,376 --> 00:02:09,855
so we would like to reveal the truth about all these robots!

41
00:02:09,855 --> 00:02:11,870
I'm intrigued right now!

42
00:02:11,870 --> 00:02:15,324
Tune in to our live broadcast this evening at 8!

43
00:02:15,324 --> 00:02:18,674
Remember to subscribe to our channel!

44
00:02:19,728 --> 00:02:22,575
What do you think he's going to say, huh?

45
00:02:22,575 --> 00:02:26,199
Could it be about that robot we saw before?

46
00:02:26,199 --> 00:02:27,401
You think?

47
00:02:27,915 --> 00:02:30,295
- Oh no, he got us!
- What?

48
00:02:30,295 --> 00:02:33,174
Going live at 8 today?! Tch!

49
00:02:33,174 --> 00:02:37,234
That dweeb is trying to sabotage the video we took of the robots!

50
00:02:39,537 --> 00:02:41,888
So tell me, what do we do next?

51
00:02:41,888 --> 00:02:43,088
I'll start thinking about that now.

52
00:02:44,088 --> 00:02:46,236
Not this again!

53
00:02:46,236 --> 00:02:48,492
Jun! It's all set up.

54
00:02:49,985 --> 00:02:51,300
Woah...

55
00:02:52,418 --> 00:02:55,634
That's awesome! Wow!

56
00:02:55,634 --> 00:02:57,247
It's a jet engine from a plane.

57
00:02:57,247 --> 00:03:01,951
It's been modified so its wind will be strong enough to blow over a Metal Cardbot.

58
00:03:01,951 --> 00:03:04,409
You're the best, Uncle Edo! This is great!

59
00:03:04,409 --> 00:03:06,324
Can't you call me your bro?! I'm not that old!

60
00:03:06,324 --> 00:03:08,486
But, what are you planning to do with this?

61
00:03:08,486 --> 00:03:12,199
It's for special training! So you can learn how to defeat Shadow X's tornado!

62
00:03:12,199 --> 00:03:13,949
Aha! Good idea!

63
00:03:13,949 --> 00:03:15,699
Let me have a go at it!

64
00:03:22,959 --> 00:03:24,788
Metal Breath, pickup!

65
00:03:26,514 --> 00:03:28,420
Mega Trucker, setup!

66
00:03:44,949 --> 00:03:46,509
Alright, alright! Let's do this!

67
00:03:46,509 --> 00:03:50,264
Okay, setting power to 80%.

68
00:03:55,704 --> 00:04:00,316
Mega Trucker will be harder to blow away since he's heavier than Blue Cop, right?

69
00:04:00,316 --> 00:04:02,760
I can handle a little spring breeze.

70
00:04:02,760 --> 00:04:05,000
Power 100%.

71
00:04:11,425 --> 00:04:15,824
Mega Trucker, use your Shoulder Shield! You gotta hang on!

72
00:04:16,223 --> 00:04:18,127
Shoulder Shield!

73
00:04:22,281 --> 00:04:24,329
Output 120%!

74
00:04:24,329 --> 00:04:25,848
I'm not backing down yet!

75
00:04:25,848 --> 00:04:27,528
Keep it up, Mega Trucker!

76
00:04:27,528 --> 00:04:30,434
This is sure to work against Shadow X!

77
00:04:38,307 --> 00:04:39,625
Shadow X!

78
00:04:39,625 --> 00:04:43,485
So you guys are training? Should've let me know! I would have helped you!

79
00:04:43,485 --> 00:04:46,802
Augh, this is a rental!

80
00:04:46,802 --> 00:04:48,747
You'll pay for the damages!

81
00:04:48,747 --> 00:04:50,341
Not my problem!

82
00:04:51,540 --> 00:04:54,485
Shall we settle the score once and for all?

83
00:04:54,485 --> 00:04:56,848
Mega Trucker, show us what you got!

84
00:04:59,925 --> 00:05:02,560
That blockhead from yesterday, huh? Ha!

85
00:05:02,560 --> 00:05:04,168
Spinning Cutter!

86
00:05:04,569 --> 00:05:06,079
Look out, Mega Trucker!

87
00:05:09,997 --> 00:05:14,613
Hahaha! You thought I'd attack from the front where you have your defenses?

88
00:05:14,613 --> 00:05:16,589
Are you really that stupid?

89
00:05:17,560 --> 00:05:19,721
I'm not done yet!

90
00:05:19,721 --> 00:05:22,250
Oh? Persistent, aren't you?

91
00:05:23,016 --> 00:05:23,956
Gotcha!

92
00:05:24,899 --> 00:05:25,898
Let go of me!

93
00:05:28,495 --> 00:05:28,995
Wait-!

94
00:05:32,134 --> 00:05:34,012
You broke my propeller!

95
00:05:37,903 --> 00:05:39,473
Come back, Mega Trucker!

96
00:05:44,495 --> 00:05:46,922
You fought hard, Mega Trucker. Get some rest.

97
00:05:47,523 --> 00:05:48,557
Jun.

98
00:05:49,189 --> 00:05:50,610
Blue Cop!

99
00:05:50,610 --> 00:05:52,485
Jun. Summon me, please.

100
00:05:52,485 --> 00:05:53,483
But...

101
00:05:53,483 --> 00:05:55,082
Please.

102
00:05:56,384 --> 00:05:57,341
Well, alright.

103
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:03,781
Metal Breath, pickup!

104
00:06:05,533 --> 00:06:06,956
Blue Cop, setup!

105
00:06:26,704 --> 00:06:29,134
Ha! You again?

106
00:06:29,134 --> 00:06:32,814
As long as there is a need to fight for justice, I will rise up time and time again!

107
00:06:32,814 --> 00:06:35,199
Wow, how heroic!

108
00:06:36,987 --> 00:06:39,163
Shadow X can't fly anymore.

109
00:06:39,163 --> 00:06:41,769
Now's your chance to close in on him and take him down.

110
00:06:41,769 --> 00:06:42,509
Roger that.

111
00:06:44,125 --> 00:06:47,951
You thought that would keep me from flying? Ha!

112
00:06:48,750 --> 00:06:50,151
Here we go!

113
00:06:52,350 --> 00:06:53,975
Yahoo!

114
00:06:55,362 --> 00:06:56,562
No way...

115
00:06:57,062 --> 00:06:58,622
He could do that?

116
00:06:59,122 --> 00:07:01,151
Haha! Coming through!

117
00:07:03,223 --> 00:07:05,399
Woah! Not bad!

118
00:07:05,682 --> 00:07:07,706
Now I'll show you something fun!

119
00:07:07,706 --> 00:07:10,548
Heli-Tornado!

120
00:07:21,680 --> 00:07:22,829
Jun! Are you alright?

121
00:07:22,829 --> 00:07:24,613
I'm okay, don't worry!

122
00:07:24,613 --> 00:07:27,788
Just hang in there. Let's get out of here for now.

123
00:07:27,788 --> 00:07:30,701
Trust me on this! Friends believe in each other.

124
00:07:34,697 --> 00:07:36,269
Friends...

125
00:07:38,480 --> 00:07:40,250
I know you can do this!

126
00:07:40,250 --> 00:07:43,225
Turn into a police car and run laps around him!

127
00:07:43,225 --> 00:07:44,449
Got it!

128
00:07:54,947 --> 00:07:56,682
What are you trying to do?!

129
00:07:56,682 --> 00:07:59,836
Blue Cop's police car mode has less air resistance,

130
00:07:59,836 --> 00:08:02,637
so it's not as easily affected by the wind!

131
00:08:04,185 --> 00:08:05,531
That piece of-!

132
00:08:08,622 --> 00:08:10,668
Just a little more! Faster!

133
00:08:14,949 --> 00:08:17,324
Wha-! What's happening?!

134
00:08:17,324 --> 00:08:21,363
He must consume a lot of energy to create a tornado that big!

135
00:08:21,363 --> 00:08:23,879
He can't keep that up for long!

136
00:08:26,358 --> 00:08:28,250
His system is overloaded!

137
00:08:28,250 --> 00:08:29,869
Get him now, Blue Cop!

138
00:08:33,239 --> 00:08:35,336
Megabolt Punch!

139
00:08:40,850 --> 00:08:42,658
Megabolt...

140
00:08:42,658 --> 00:08:43,648
Punch!

141
00:08:43,748 --> 00:08:45,875
Aaaaah!

142
00:08:56,539 --> 00:08:59,517
No way... my Heli-Tornado...

143
00:09:00,658 --> 00:09:02,775
You did it, Blue Cop!

144
00:09:02,775 --> 00:09:06,321
A true friend is someone who doesn't give up, even when things get tough.

145
00:09:06,321 --> 00:09:07,528
Someone you can count on.

146
00:09:08,129 --> 00:09:10,730
Friend? Heh.

147
00:09:11,230 --> 00:09:14,234
Was that... what I didn't have?

148
00:09:14,533 --> 00:09:16,322
I lost. As promised,

149
00:09:16,322 --> 00:09:18,063
I will become your underling.

150
00:09:23,086 --> 00:09:25,688
Not an underling. But a friend.

151
00:09:26,807 --> 00:09:27,868
Sealing complete!

152
00:09:27,868 --> 00:09:28,883
Good job.

153
00:09:29,849 --> 00:09:31,480
But what are you going to do now?

154
00:09:31,980 --> 00:09:33,182
Whaddya mean?

155
00:09:33,182 --> 00:09:36,311
Have you forgotten? We're going live tonight.

156
00:09:38,700 --> 00:09:39,543
Oh no!

157
00:10:02,548 --> 00:10:05,942
So you see? All the robot sightings were actually made up

158
00:10:05,942 --> 00:10:08,673
using custom made miniatures and special effects!

159
00:10:08,874 --> 00:10:10,355
Hey, hang on!

160
00:10:10,355 --> 00:10:14,437
We really saw it! It was a robot as big as a house, and flying around!

161
00:10:14,437 --> 00:10:16,404
Oh, that?

162
00:10:16,404 --> 00:10:18,094
Well, take a look!

163
00:10:18,094 --> 00:10:23,890
Ahem. This robot is a 1 to 1 scale model made to order by a film studio.

164
00:10:23,890 --> 00:10:25,923
What?! A model?!

165
00:10:25,923 --> 00:10:31,527
Of course! It's made of styrofoam, so it's very light, you see? Heheh.

166
00:10:31,527 --> 00:10:34,749
I put it in the warehouse, but it must have blown away in the wind.

167
00:10:34,749 --> 00:10:36,673
I'm sorry for the commotion.

168
00:10:37,100 --> 00:10:39,033
So everyone, this was our live broadcast,

169
00:10:39,033 --> 00:10:42,798
"I Saw Mysterious Robots Flying Around the Docks!"

170
00:10:42,798 --> 00:10:45,134
Make sure to tune in to our next episode!

171
00:10:46,048 --> 00:10:48,370
And please remember to subscribe!

172
00:10:49,148 --> 00:10:53,735
Urgh... do you think you can fool me with those lies?

173
00:10:53,735 --> 00:10:59,225
I'll get my hands on some evidence no matter what it takes! You better watch out, Jun!

